# Cloud Service Models

## 1. Infrastructure as a Service (IaaS)

AWS provides:

- Virtual Machines
- CPU
- RAM
- Storage
- Networking

You manage:

- Operating System
- Java
- Spring Boot
- Database
- Application

### Example

- Amazon EC2

---

## 2. Platform as a Service (PaaS)

AWS manages:

- Infrastructure
- Operating System
- Runtime

You manage:

- Application
- Business Logic

### Example

- AWS Elastic Beanstalk

---

## 3. Software as a Service (SaaS)

Provider manages everything.

Users simply use the software.

### Examples

- Gmail
- Google Docs
- Slack
- Microsoft 365

---

# Spring Boot Deployment Example

## Deploy on EC2

You install:

- Java
- Maven
- Spring Boot Application

Cloud Model:

> Infrastructure as a Service (IaaS)

---

## Deploy on Elastic Beanstalk

Upload the application.

AWS manages:

- Server
- Runtime
- Infrastructure

Cloud Model:

> Platform as a Service (PaaS)

